# Stop being Chaotic -- leave Chaotic for True Neutral by the ordinary
# "Issue Request" command, as a Chaotic character whose desired alignment is
# Neutral. This is the leaving-Chaotic half of bd inc-r6ae;
# tools/check_align_leave_chaotic_play.sh reads it.
#
# WHAT IS BEING OBSERVED. A Chaotic character who commits a non-chaotic act
# decays the law/chaos score (alignLC) in Character::AlignedAct
# (src/Prayer.cpp) and, once the score falls below +20, must clear AL_CHAOTIC.
# Before the fix the committed-chaotic branch pinned the score with
# max(30, alignLC) where its good/evil twin used min(30, alignLC), so the score
# could never fall below 20 and the character stayed Chaotic however many acts
# were committed. This run leaves Chaotic.
#
# THE CHARACTER is tools/keys/chargen.keys' standard orc barbarian, but with
# Chaotic Neutral chosen at generation rather than Neutral. Generation sets
# alignLC to +50 for a Chaotic character (src/Create.cpp:473-474). He carries no
# Diplomacy and Intimidate +6, so Creature::Request (src/Social.cpp:1189-1190)
# offers "Use Intimidate?" and fires the COERCION aligned act
# (AL_NONCHAOTIC|AL_LAWFUL, magnitude 3). The AL_NONCHAOTIC half is what decays.
#
# THE DESIRED ALIGNMENT is stated with the character sheet's own
# '[D] Alignment' command (src/Managers.cpp:2315-2322) and set to Neutral.
# This matters: AlignedAct clamps the score with min(30, alignLC) only while
# the character does NOT desire Chaotic (the `if (!(dAlign & AL_CHAOTIC))`
# guard). Left desiring Chaotic, the clamp is skipped and the score would not
# change.
#
# THE VICTIM is a human conjured by wizard mode, one square east, and frozen;
# every coercion is the ordinary command. Each coercion aborts at the "Direct
# Creature Where" prompt, so no TRIED flag is set and the same victim serves
# again.
#
# THE COUNT, from the arithmetic: alignLC 50 -> *7/10 -> 35 -> min(30) -> 30
# -> *7/10 -> 21 -> min(30) -> 21 -> *7/10 -> 14 -> min(30) -> 14, which is
# below 20, so the THIRD coercion clears AL_CHAOTIC and the game prints
# "You are now True Neutral.". Four are sent for margin; the fourth neither
# moves a flag nor prints. With the defect (max(30,...)) the score pins at 30
# and no count ever leaves Chaotic.
#
# Determinism: seed 1, tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat.

a
n
y
@choose "Orc"
@choose "Orc (Standard)"
@choose "Barbarian"
a
@choose "Chaotic Neutral"
a
a

RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y

y

RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y

.*2
@dump:arrival

d
@until "Desired Alignment" D
@choose "Neutral"
ESC

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
@expect "Freeze Monsters"
DOWN*10
@expect "all monsters are denied their"
SPACE
@expect "Wizard Mode Options"
ESC
@dump:frozen

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Humans"
@choose "human"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:summoned

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Use Intimidate?" y
@dump:coerce1
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Use Intimidate?" y
@dump:coerce2
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Use Intimidate?" y
@dump:coerce3
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Use Intimidate?" y
@dump:coerce4
@choose "Go To Location"
